(NORTHWIND ENERGY - ANNUAL BOARD REVIEW) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Northwind Energy closed the financial year with revenue below the guidance issued at the) Tj T*
(start of the period. The shortfall was concentrated in the third quarter and was) Tj T*
(attributed to delayed grid connection approvals rather than to any loss of customers to) Tj T*
(competitors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Maya Ellison, an engineer at Northwind Energy, led the preparation of the remediation) Tj T*
(plan and presented it to the board in November. Her assessment was that the delays were) Tj T*
(procedural rather than technical.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Tomas Reyes, the chief financial officer of Northwind Energy, supported the plan and) Tj T*
(took responsibility for the reporting changes it requires. He noted that the company had) Tj T*
(no single view of connection milestones before this year.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Kestrel Grid remains the largest counterparty of Northwind Energy by contract value. The) Tj T*
(transmission agreement between the two firms was renewed during the year for a further) Tj T*
(two years on substantially the same commercial terms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The board recorded a concentration risk: Kestrel Grid represents a large enough share of) Tj T*
(revenue that the loss or renegotiation of the transmission agreement would be) Tj T*
(significant. No action was proposed this year.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
